## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical design of a CKNE-aware serverless scheduler that balances latency guarantees with multi-tenant fairness under dynamic CKNE scoring.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE-driven per-tenant concurrency budgets and burst allowances
- Warm/cold-start pool management with eviction semantics
- Minute-by-minute degradation loop and capacity reallocation logic
- Comprehensive telemetry, SLA verification, and preemption rules

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo quota calculator
function quotaForTenant(ckne, base) {
  const soft = Math.max(1, Math.floor(base * ckne));
  const burst = Math.floor(soft * (1 + ckne));
  const coldPool = Math.ceil(ckne * 10);
  return { soft, burst, coldPool };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
CKNE-aware caching for multi-tenant real-time pipelines is a plausible, high-impact reliability topic that blends performance with health signals.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant TTL policy driven by CKNE health
- Cache stampede guards with jitter and request coalescing
- Edge prefetch/invalidation triggered by health trend

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal TTL decision helper
function ttlForTenant(baseTTL, ckne) {
  const health = ckne?.health ?? 1;
  const factor = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, health));
  const ttl = Math.round(baseTTL * (1 - (1 - factor) * 0.5));
  return Math.max(30, Math.min(3600, ttl));
}
```

