## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-QoS mapping: dynamic quota allocation, eviction policies, and prefetch budgets
- Real-time rebalancing cadence with latency guarantees
- Telemetry-driven fairness mechanisms and failure mode handling under multi-tenant load

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo CKNE-aware rebalancer (simplified)
function rebalance() {
  const cknes = collectCKNEScores(); // {tenant, ckne}
  cknes.forEach(t => {
    const quota = calculateQuota(t.ckne);
    const evictionRate = calculateEvictionRate(t.ckne);
    const prefetchBudget = calculatePrefetchBudget(t.ckne);
    updateTenantConfig(t.tenant, quota, evictionRate, prefetchBudget);
  });
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Real-world BI workloads multiplex dozens to thousands of tenants; CKNE-driven concurrency and memory control is critical for SLOs and fair sharing.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-resource mapping: concurrency, memory budget, spill/IO throttling
- Per-tenant quotas and dynamic reallocation cadence
- Fairness guarantees and explicit preemption rules
- Telemetry hooks and feedback for regret-free adjustment

## Code Example
```javascript
function allocate(tenants){
  // normalize CKNE 0-1 to weight, compute quotas
  const total = tenants.reduce((a,t)=>a+t.ckne,0);
  tenants.forEach(t=>{ t.alloc = t.ckne/total; });
  return tenants;
}
```

